  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="340e4482-d55a-5233-bad7-4796a961c454" activityNameId="8a537c97-99c2-5e54-8318-ae3f26b5ec38" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation system, Pflegezentrum Witikon</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation system, Pflegezentrum Witikon
Disposal of a ventilation system for a residential care home with apartments, kitchen, cafe/restaurant, multi-purpose hall, laundry and car park. The inventory is based on a building with a total heated gross floor area of 11358 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 74580 m3/h, total weight of the components: 30520 kg/Unit, building with a specific air flow rate of 6.6 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. Data from call of bid including components for air handling units, ducts including insulation, air valves, roof-hoods, dampers, fire dampers, silencers. The data represent a ductwork mainly made of galvanized steel and includes air handling units mainly with heat recovery. System with central air handling units. Building without ground heat exchanger.;
UUID: 041e12fb-6361-40ef-9a9f-5e383f3dae12
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_041e12fb-6361-40ef-9a9f-5e383f3dae12.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
